# What `maps_merge.py setup --apply --local-attributes` writes into
# .git/info/attributes of ONE clone. It overrides the committed .gitattributes
# for that clone only.
#
# Do NOT put these lines in the shared, committed .gitattributes. When an
# attribute names a merge driver that is not configured, Git does a plain
# line-by-line text merge, not "binary, pick a side". Anyone who has not run
# setup would then get MAPS files and models text-merged without warning.
#
# The model lines are only valid together with the mlAutoMerge driver, which
# setup configures when it is given --matlabroot.
*.MAPS merge=maps diff=maps
*.maps merge=maps diff=maps
*.mdl  binary merge=mlAutoMerge
*.slx  binary merge=mlAutoMerge
